{"id": "EUVD-2026-81928", "enisaUuid": "1b11dba2-4d49-3b15-8ffc-646750a6a0a5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlibceph: validate banner payload length\n\nWhen parsing the Ceph messenger v2 protocol banner, the `payload_len` field\nis decoded from the banner prefix. If a client sends a banner with a\n`payload_len` of 0, the kernel sets up a 0-length socket read. This\nviolates an invariant in the state machine, triggering a warning in\n`populate_in_iter()`:\n\n------------[ cut here ]------------\n!iov_iter_count(&con->v2.in_iter)\nWARNING: net/ceph/messenger_v2.c:3129 at populate_in_iter\nnet/ceph/messenger_v2.c:3129 [inline], CPU#1: kworker/1:3/5070\nWARNING: net/ceph/messenger_v2.c:3129 at ceph_con_v2_try_read+0x6634/0x6810\nnet/ceph/messenger_v2.c:3159, CPU#1: kworker/1:3/5070\n...\nCall Trace:\n <TASK>\n ceph_con_workfn+0x1f5/0x14a0 net/ceph/messenger.c:1575\n process_one_work kernel/workqueue.c:3322 [inline]\n process_scheduled_works+0xa8e/0x14e0 kernel/workqueue.c:3405\n worker_thread+0xa47/0xfb0 kernel/workqueue.c:3486\n kthread+0x388/0x470 kernel/kthread.c:436\n ret_from_fork+0x514/0xb70 arch/x86/kernel/process.c:158\n ret_from_fork_asm+0x1a/0x30 arch/x86/entry/entry_64.S:245\n </TASK>\n\nAccording to the msgr2 protocol specification, the banner payload is\nexpected to contain at least two 64-bit integers (`server_feat` and\n`server_req_feat`). Therefore, `payload_len` must be at least 16 bytes.\n\nFix this by adding a check in `process_banner_prefix()` to reject a\n`payload_len` smaller than 16 bytes. This prevents the 0-length read and\ncorrectly aborts the connection with a protocol error.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:05:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:57:24", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/279c0852999fd2384f4a88155091a99e81f96873", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6cf666e47f2b51d5a887ec8a3226cde951757d27", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b2e62a7655d347a845a91155610ddae11daffc6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1b937ff24b19e69aa7fb1b0f46a74d4c9668692", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d1c6f228854aa89844fd0152d7ed7ac72a55e89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c77633a9595658210a6e216a071e5a396a0835a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f374967fcdf04001c9b66df1c19106fa83cd91f7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90067", "GHSA-prv5-g54g-rmhh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.67, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06b08981-8184-39f7-b74f-2d22eb15aa97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "1f05be3a-94c6-371a-8dfd-8a670d0ebe50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "20ee1994-528c-3a08-97fd-b641e2433fd8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "259d5bb2-156c-3395-bb7d-8d786864d9df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd1a677cad994021b19665ed476aea63f5d54f31 <c1b937ff24b19e69aa7fb1b0f46a74d4c9668692"}, {"id": "32e0ce05-29d4-3daf-8bee-93fb6b52a470", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd1a677cad994021b19665ed476aea63f5d54f31 <279c0852999fd2384f4a88155091a99e81f96873"}, {"id": "5d02737e-6e1b-3b22-bbef-6f9aad0cae2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.11"}, {"id": "7475ec2a-e9c6-39e4-82b6-ca0304d24962", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd1a677cad994021b19665ed476aea63f5d54f31 <6d1c6f228854aa89844fd0152d7ed7ac72a55e89"}, {"id": "7fab6a0f-9daf-3a10-93a4-c8d4b0923d46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "8248fe5c-bbf1-3155-974a-6013cd7937ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version":